---
description: WinUI shell and KuroShell.Core
globs: KuroShell/**
alwaysApply: false
---
Put logic in `KuroShell.Core` with tests; keep XAML code-behind thin.
The shell supervises the engine process; it does not own hold-to-talk hotkey logic.
Never register a global hotkey from the shell project.
Only `CapsulePlacement.cs` (when present) positions the capsule HUD.
No `async void` except through existing helpers.
IPC DTO changes start in `contract/` once the protocol crate lands (phase 15).
Do not embed tool routing or phrase tables in the shell.
Run shell tests via `cargo xtask gate fast` (includes dotnet when shell changes).